gence from Solo match predictions, value props and trending Full archive from Edge all available historical seasons across every sport Market intelligence from Edge consensus and fair price, divergence, line movement and closing lines Real time from Pro WebSocket push instead of polling, plus an SLA Free covers every sport; Solo is 1, Trio is 3, and Edge opens all of them again. Unified schema One envelope across every sport. Integrate once, cover everything. WebSocket live feed Live score push on Pro+. socket.io rooms by sport, league, match. Confidence scoring Every field exposes its own data quality and freshness so your app handles uncertainty. Every sport Football (Soccer), basketball, baseball, NFL, NHL, F1, MMA, cricket, under one key. 250 free / day Enough to build and evaluate the whole API against real data (500/day with GitHub connected). No credit card, no trial clock. No credit card Sign up with your email. No card on file until you actually need more volume. Not sure which plan? Price it at your scale. Drag the sliders to your real numbers. We&#x27;ll recommend a plan and show what the same usage costs on a raw-data API. vs BallDontLie vs The Rundown vs The Odds API vs API-Sports vs Sportmonks vs Sportradar vs SportsData.io vs football-data.org vs API-Football vs the ESPN API vs OpticOdds vs MySportsFeeds vs TheSportsDB vs OddsJam Monthly active users 10,000 API requests per user / day 1 Sports covered 3 sports 10,000 requests/day on Big Balls Sports Data. A full matchup page is 1 call here vs 8 raw calls per sport on BallDontLie . Big Balls Sports Data $49 /mo Trio plan · All sports, one subscription BallDontLie $119.97 /mo 3 × GOAT Save $70.97 /mo ( $851.64 /yr) AND skip building the assembly layer. ✗ Pre-assembled matchup responses (you call and join ~8 endpoints yourself) ✗ Elo predictions and win probabilities ✗ xG shot maps ✗ Player headshots ✗ Confirmed lineups with formations ✗ Cross-sport unified schema (each sport is a separate integration AND subscription) Request volume 1 Big Balls call = 8 raw BallDontLie calls to assemble the same matchup page — per sport . At your scale that&#x27;s 10,000 vs 240,000 requests/day. Raw BallDontLie pricing covers the data subscription only. The assembly layer, intelligence features, and cross-sport unification are engineering time you build and maintain . BallDontLie price = raw data subscription only. Assembly layer, intelligence features, and cross-sport unification are not included at any tier. Pricing verified 2026-05-28 . Priced per sport, rate-limited per minute. Each sport is a separate subscription. How we stack up Three honest comparisons against the names you&#x27;re probably evaluating us against. Full breakdowns on each competitor page. vs The Odds API Confirmed lineups and injuries Big Balls Sports Data Included, one request The Odds API Not available Full The Odds API comparison → vs Sportradar Elo predictions and win probability Big Balls Sports Data Included, one request Sportradar no Elo model Full Sportradar comparison → The plans Free includes the current season. Solo and Trio include up to five seasons for the sport(s) you pick. Edge and Pro include all available history across every sport, plus deeper stats, predictions, and derived odds intelligence. Free $0 forever Any sport · Any sport, current + most-recent season · 250 requests / day (500 with GitHub) · 100 requests / min burst · Scores, standings, stats Start free → Solo $39 $19 / month 1 sport, your pick · 1 sport, your pick — see live depth below · Up to 5 seasons joined to results · Match predictions, value props and trending — the model layer · 10,000 requests / day · 300 requests / min burst · Change your sport once every 30 days Get Solo → Trio Most popular $99 $49 / month 3 sports, your pick · Any 3 sports, your pick — see live depth below · All historical seasons joined to results · 25,000 requests / day · 500 requests / min burst · Change your 3 sports (as one set) once every 30 days Get Trio → Edge $299 $149 / month All sports · All available history · Full stats depth for cricket, hockey, baseball, NFL, and NBA — soccer expanding · Fair-price edges across the market — expanding sport by sport · Model-ready team features — rest/fatigue (days_rest, back-to-back, last-5 form) and against-the-spread splits by home/away and favorite/underdog · Derived odds intelligence — consensus, fair price, divergence, and line movement · 100,000 requests / day · 1,500 requests / min burst Get Edge → Pro $999 $299 / month All sports · Everything in Edge · NFL play-by-play — full EPA + win probability event log · WebSocket / real-time push · Priority support + SLA · 200,000 requests / day · 3,000 requests / min burst · Licensed raw odds board (coming, once the redistribution license lands) Get Pro → Enterprise Custom contact sales All sports · Every sport, full history · Bulk export, deep archive, odds intelligence, play-by-play · Custom volume, SLA, dedicated support Talk to us → What Solo and Trio actually get, per sport Computed live from what&#x27;s actually in the database right now — not a promise. Some sports only have one season on record today; this says so plainly instead of selling history that doesn&#x27;t exist yet. Sport Solo / Trio history Soccer Current + 4 prior seasons Basketball Current + 4 prior seasons American Football Current + 4 prior seasons Baseball Current + 4 prior seasons Ice Hockey Current + 4 prior seasons Cricket Current + 4 prior seasons MMA Current + 4 prior seasons Boxing Current + 1 prior season Formula 1 Current season only Coming soon Not priced yet. Tell us you&#x27;re interested and we&#x27;ll reach out when pricing is set. Production Coming soon Higher volume, dedicated infrastructure, and an SLA for production traffic. Email Notify me Odds Board Coming soon A live, book-by-book odds board across every market we carry. Email Notify me Enter your email, get your API key We&#x27;ll email you a one-time sign-in link. No password, no credit card , your key is ready in the dashboard the moment you click. Email Get your API key No password needed. We&#x27;ll email you a one-time sign-in link. Prefer to sign up with GitHub, Google, or X? Use the full signup page instead. Frequently asked How do rate limits work? Two buckets: per-minute (sliding window) + per-day (UTC fixed window). Every response carries X-RateLimit-Remaining; 429 responses include a Retry-After header. Can I downgrade or cancel anytime? Yes, manage your plan from the dashboard or the Stripe Customer Portal. Downgrades take effect at the next billing cycle. What counts as one request? One HTTP request to any /v1/* endpoint. Fields inside a response don&#x27;t count separately. Events received over the WebSocket feed do NOT count against your rate limit. What if I exceed my plan? The gateway returns 429. You can upgrade instantly, new limits apply immediately. The sports data API built for ballers. Add to Google preferred sources Sports & Leagues Soccer Football Premier League La Liga Serie A Bundesliga Ligue 1 Champions League MLS World Cup 2026 Africa Cup of Nations CONCACAF Gold Cup Copa América Euro Championship UEFA Nations League Basketball NBA NCAA Basketball WNBA American Football NFL NCAAF (FBS & FCS) Baseball MLB Ice Hockey NHL Cricket MMA UFC Boxing Formula 1 Product Docs API Reference Pricing Coverage API Status Sports coverage League codes What&#x27;s new Blog About Datasets Injuries Live NBA Props Live NHL Props Live NBA Shot Chart MLB Odds MLB Pitch Data Free Sports API Tools Odds Calculator Parlay Calculator No-Vig Calculator Hedge Calculator Kelly Criterion Calculator Tutorials Fantasy hockey app Fantasy basketball app Soccer xG app Cricket app NFL fantasy football API tutorial NFL scouting tool NFL conditions analytics tool NFL betting model API tutorial NFL live game center API tutorial NCAAF scoreboard and live game center How to build college football rankings and conference standings NCAAF fantasy foo